  "ai_overview": {
    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Both ACE inhibitors (ending in -pril, such as lisinopril) and ARBs (ending in -sartan , such as losartan) are equally recommended as Class I first-line options for treating primary hypertension.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "Both ACE inhibitors (ending in -pril, such as lisinopril) and ARBs (ending in -sartan , such as losartan) are equally recommended as Class I first-line options for treating primary hypertension"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Large-scale real-world studies (such as the LEGEND-HTN network study) and clinical trials show that both drug classes lower blood pressure and offer comparable cardiovascular effectiveness (no significant difference in heart attack, stroke, or heart failure risk). However, they differ in how they work and their side-effect profiles:",
        "reference_indexes": [
          2
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Mechanism of Action"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "ACE Inhibitors: Block the enzyme that converts angiotensin I into angiotensin II (a potent vasoconstrictor). They also cause a buildup of bradykinin, which can trigger side effects .",
            "reference_indexes": [
              3
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "ARBs (Angiotensin II Receptor Blockers): Block angiotensin II directly from binding to its cellular receptors (AT1 receptors) without affecting bradykinin levels."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Side Effects and Tolerability"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "ACE Inhibitors: Have a higher rate of adverse effects, most notably a persistent dry, scratchy cough (~10% of patients) and a risk of serious or life-threatening facial/throat swelling ().",
            "reference_indexes": [
              4,
              5,
              6
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "ARBs: Have a significantly better safety and tolerability profile. They carry a much lower risk of dry cough (~3%) and rare angioedema, making them the preferred alternative or first-line pick for patients sensitive to ACE inhibitors."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Shared Precautions"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Pregnancy: Both classes are strictly contraindicated during pregnancy (teratogenic/harmful to the fetus)."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Kidney & Electrolyte Risks: Both can cause elevated potassium levels (hyperkalemia) or acute changes in kidney function, and they should never be combined with each other ."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Current clinical evidence leans toward preferentially starting with an ARB over an ACE inhibitor due to better patient adherence and fewer bothersome or dangerous side effects, though individual choice depends on medical history, insurance/cost, and provider preference. You can read more about how they compare on the American Academy of Family Physicians Blog _3VPyasXgMbDliLMP9eHnkAQ_18 or via the National Kidney Foundation Guide _3VPyasXgMbDliLMP9eHnkAQ_19 .",
        "reference_indexes": [
          7
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like to narrow this down, let me know:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Are you or a loved one starting a new prescription or switching from an ACE inhibitor due to a cough?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Are there any other conditions present, such as diabetes or chronic kidney disease?"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
